UNIT is_number
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 4aa5cea5898114eaa972bfdabdbef768883df47088f71c660abd5ef57181df4f
SIG isNumber(num: any): boolean
NOTE default export
ABI f64=number (finite ⇔ neither NaN nor ±Infinity; -0 is a distinct finite value); text=UTF-16 string; bool=boolean; none=null|undefined.
  "primitive" (R1, R2, R4) = typeof; boxed wrappers are typeof 'object'. "parses as a number" (R2) = numeric coercion of the
  trimmed string (+s / Number(s)); "trimmed" = String.prototype.trim.
ENVELOPE js widens the primary's envelope to any JS value: objects, arrays, functions and boxed wrappers are in scope here (R3/R4).
DEPENDS-ON none
PROVENANCE the shipped @rederive/is-number src (runs/js/emit_1.mjs), verified-recompose quorum 3/3, differential 400/400.
